ounty&rsquo;s 6 grids came in under 90% of normal in August to September in 40 of 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. In 2025 that pair ran 40% of normal on the middle, while June to July hit 167%. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, with grid 25353 at 51%. A preliminary estimate puts August to September 2026 at 201.7 on grid 25353, from NOAA rain and not RMA&rsquo;s final index.</p>"}
